{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013043-could-you-do-a-pokemon-style-world-of-darkness-horror-game","id":1013043,"title":"Could you do a Pokemon style world of darkness horror game ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T00:02:07-08:00","id":1013043,"title":"Could you do a Pokemon style world of darkness horror game ?","content":"I was thinking about doing a all humans campaign that would be kind of like Pokemon or maybe Yokai Watch. Where the players would befriend spirits and help them defeat other spirits and battle each other. The players could get the spirits attached to simple devices like special key chains or maybe even a cell phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T00:15:26-08:00","id":1013047,"title":"","content":"If you're just talking about the rules, then yeah I see why not. It would however, mean the player controlling a spirit during battles, and spirit rules aren't quite player-frieny as I recall (but not unplayable). You'll also have to tweak Manifestation and Essence rules.<br /> <br /> If the setting and atmosphere of CoD games is included as well... it'll end up less like Pokemon and more like Shin Megami Tensei. The Devil Survivor series to be precise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T01:36:32-08:00","id":1013068,"title":"","content":"Funny coincidence, but not so long ago I had an idea for how to turn Cardcaptor Sakura into a legitimate game in Chronicles of Darkness, with some not insignificant groundwork from Mage 2e. See if you can draw from that too, seeing as Mages do have spells that affect essence, spirits wnd such, and there a artefacts that normal people can use with spells as an innate part of them.<br /> <br /> That, or make it an experiment the God-Machine is running as an excuse...or some other force. The world id your oyster here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T06:14:50-08:00","id":1013115,"title":"","content":"Could have a pack where the players are wolf-bloods and the rest of the pack are spirits that they've caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:33:37-08:00","id":1013184,"title":"","content":"The players could be Sleepwalkers or Proximi working for the Mysterium. Their mission would be to capture rogue ephemeral beings and other monsters and bind them to magical objects for study and safe-keeping. When they do a good job, they are allowed to keep some of these bound entities as allies.<br /> <br /> For mechanics, you probably don't need to change a lot. Just use a variant of the Familiar Manifestation from Mage, or invent a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:41:48-08:00","id":1013228,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3932_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3932\" data-vbnamecard=\"3932\">The young man in the cafe</a> has rules for Heroes as Beast tamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:01:42-08:00","id":1013241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013043-could-you-do-a-pokemon-style-world-of-darkness-horror-game?p=1013228#post1013228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3932_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3932\" data-vbnamecard=\"3932\">The young man in the cafe</a> has rules for Heroes as Beast tamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do need to work on that some more. Right now it is just the bare bones of the beast tamer rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:37:55-08:00","id":1013261,"title":"","content":"Through use of the goblin market's slave rules and a custom token to act as a 'pokeball' I think it'd be rather easy. At least that is how I considered it in the past. This method could work for all denizens of the world of darkness - yes even humans. Just sadly with this method because of the mechanics of tokens the trainers would have to be changeling. Or the ST could just hand wave an explanation and use human friendly tokens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:38:07-08:00","id":1013329,"title":"","content":"There is no need for hand wave too much. Tokens and Goblin Fruits are so diverse that isn't extraordinary for one given type to ignore any given rule. Actually, this kind of device can be worked in a huge number of different ways, Hedge's Tokens, God-Machine's experiments, Athlantean Artifacts or other kind of work from a Mage, a strange outgrow from somewhere in the Shadow, or things ever stranger.<br /> <br /> I worked for some time at an adaptation of Pok\u00e9mon proper to CoD. It is underway, but I can see if I put some of it here, if I can still find it.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, the greatest problem is to how you'll deal with balance with the rules of the beings you're using. Be it for ephemeral or physical beings, splat-explained or utterly mysterious, the game have already sound rules for almost everything you can imagine. Goblins, Pandorans, Zombies, Spirits, Angels, Ghosts, and much more that you can use, either as-is or just the rules. They are simple, broad, easy to use and solid as rules. But they were never meant for PCs hands, so they're not so simple to balance. You'll have to set some baselines, like the Familiar Merit, but also be quite cautious with the final sheet, specially powers.<br /> <br /> Setting/Game style-wise, I go with 21C Hermit. Shin Megami Tensei can be a far more reasonable inspiration if you want to keep with the horror theme. All the games of the series and its spin-offs can lend inspiration to a given take on the World of Darkness. You can right-away implement the Devil Summoner Program in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:32:14-08:00","id":1013747,"title":"","content":"The werewolf chroniclers guide has a merit that gives werewolves their own spirit entourage. Spirit supremacy- From three level 1 spirits at level 1, to having 15 ranks available (but with only one rank five possible at a time) at level five. <br /> <br /> When I read that my first thought was that it was the pokemon merit. <br /> <br /> Also something to keep in mind is that ephemeral beings are valid for social merits like retainers, allies, contacts, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:25:18-08:00","id":1013779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013043-could-you-do-a-pokemon-style-world-of-darkness-horror-game?p=1013747#post1013747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also something to keep in mind is that ephemeral beings are valid for social merits like retainers, allies, contacts, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Staff. <sub>characters</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:48:21-08:00","id":1013789,"title":"","content":"The only problem I can see with this idea is that the Exarchs have arranged for it to be a Supernal truth that you gotta catch 'em all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T08:52:18-08:00","id":1013791,"title":"","content":"Null Mysteriis - Gotta Catalog Them All?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}